+# Batch 36 — Step 1 authoring evidence
+
+Run: `advanced-qft-supersymmetry-build-2026-10-23`  
+Scope: `qftx-defects-and-topological-operators` and its examples companion.
+
+## Scope and plan reconciliation
+
+Read the batch task, generic beta scaffold brief, run owner direction, the complete assigned design section in `research/plan-advanced-qft-and-supersymmetry-track.md`, the corresponding `research/plan-spec.json` rows, the exact proposed item contracts, and the relevant specialist note `research/advanced-qft-supersymmetry-2026-10-23/research-symmetries-defects-anomalies.md`.
+
+The canonical plan row and assigned design agree on the A/B IDs, title, category, physics library, order 992, companion, and required pages `qftx-defect-fusion-mathematics` and `qftx-susy-algebra-and-multiplets`. The plan has `items: []`; the design and proposed inventory name the two exact A-page definitions `def-aqft-topological-defect` and `def-aqft-topological-interface`. Per the binding owner direction, the empty plan arrays are authoring placeholders, so the two specified A items are entered in the batch manifest. The same direction requires substantive B-page examples, so this batch adds two finite-model examples and one counterexample on the assigned B page. This fills only batch 36's pair; the shared plan remains untouched.
+
+The assigned design scope is preserved: define embedded defects and interfaces with an isotopy-invariance test, distinguish endodefects from interfaces between different theories, require invertibility and observable preservation for an internal symmetry, and do not infer physical realization from categorical fusion data or BPS algebra. The interface definition cites the earlier in-pair defect definition because it reuses its correlator and isotopy criterion; this is the one additional item edge beyond the proposed empty `proposed_deps` fields. Its level is therefore recomputed from the actual edge.
+
+## Dependency inventory and inspected suppliers
+
+The recorded page-level dependency level is 3: batch 36 requires batches 15 (level 0) and 29 (level 2). The item graph after authoring is expected to be:
+
+| Item | In-run item suppliers | Level |
+|---|---|---:|
+| `def-aqft-topological-defect` | none | 0 |
+| `def-aqft-topological-interface` | `def-aqft-topological-defect` | 1 |
+| `ex-aqft-z2-topological-defect-finite-quantum-mechanics` | `def-aqft-topological-defect` | 1 |
+| `ex-aqft-invertible-interface-between-finite-quantum-mechanics` | `def-aqft-topological-interface` | 2 |
+| `cex-aqft-topological-interface-not-symmetry` | `def-aqft-topological-interface` | 2 |
+
